# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RidgeLine — configuration template
# Copy to .env, fill what you have, and start. Everything below can begin EMPTY:
# the local demo runs with zero credentials and marks every unmet prerequisite
# visibly on Settings → Connection status.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Core app ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Public base URL used in customer-facing links (booking links, webhooks).
# Local demo default is fine; set the deployed origin in production.
APP_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Database connection.
# Local demo (SQLite, zero setup):
DATABASE_URL="file:./db/custom.db"
# Neon / any PostgreSQL — run `bun run db:use-postgres` first to flip the schema
# provider, then point this at your connection string:
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxxx.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require"

# Signs staff session cookies (HMAC). Generate locally on first bootstrap:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# If unset in development, a deterministic dev secret is used (never in production).
SESSION_SECRET=

# Encrypts provider OAuth tokens at rest (AES-256-GCM). Same generation command.
# If unset in development, a deterministic dev key is used (never in production).
TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ── Staff sign-in (OIDC) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Staff authentication and per-contractor GHL authorization are separate flows.
# Local demo sign-in uses seeded roles (password "demo"). Provide these to move
# staff login to your identity provider:
OIDC_ISSUER_URL=
OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── GoHighLevel (marketplace app) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# From https://marketplace.gohighlevel.com — your app's credentials.
# Unlocks: OAuth install per location, calendar sync, SMS/email sending,
# estimate status sync via webhooks.
GHL_CLIENT_ID=
GHL_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Must match the redirect URI registered on the GHL app:
GHL_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/api/connections/ghl/callback
# Secret used to verify inbound webhook signatures (HMAC-SHA256 over raw bytes).
# Re-verify the exact header name + scheme against the current GHL docs when
# configuring — recorded in docs/ghl-installation-guide.md.
GHL_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Jobber (optional payment connector) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Unlocks payment/refund matching for contractors using Jobber quotes+payments.
JOBBER_CLIENT_ID=
JOBBER_CLIENT_SECRET=
JOBBER_REDIRECT_URI=

# ── Go engine (services/engine-go) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The high-performance webhook ingest + queue half of the stack. Optional in
# the local demo; see docs/go-engine.md. Full inventory: ENGINE_* in
# services/engine-go/internal/config/config.go.
# ENGINE_URL=http://localhost:8088
# ENGINE_PORT=8088
# ENGINE_REQUIRE_SIGNATURE=true
# ENGINE_WORKERS=8
# ENGINE_QUEUE_CAPACITY=4096
# ENGINE_LOG_FORMAT=text
# ENGINE_LOG_LEVEL=info

# ── Notes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# • Nothing above needs to be pasted into chat. Secrets go to env or a deploy
#   secret manager; token values are stored encrypted per location.
# • The bootstrap generates nothing into this file — you own it.
# • Connection status screen tracks: passed / failed / awaiting configuration
#   per check, so "configured" and "verified live" are visibly distinct.

# ── Go engine: GoHighLevel stack + durable store + AI brain ───────────────────

# GoHighLevel API v2 (Private Integration Token). Without a token the engine's
# executor stays in DRY-RUN: every intent is planned and logged, nothing sends.
# GHL_ACCESS_TOKEN=pit-xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx
# GHL_LOCATION_ID=your-subaccount-id
# GHL_API_BASE=https://services.leadconnectorhq.com
# GHL_DRY_RUN=false

# Durable Postgres mirror for the engine (journal + contacts + action audit).
# Same instance as the app or a dedicated one; migrations run on boot.
# DATABASE_URL_GO="postgres://user:pass@127.0.0.1:5432/convert?sslmode=disable"
# (the engine reads DATABASE_URL when pointed at Postgres; the file: SQLite URL
#  above is app-only and simply disables the mirror)

# Engine admin token (guards /v1/rules PUT and GHL write proxies).
# ENGINE_ADMIN_TOKEN=

# z.ai brain (OpenAI-compatible chat completions). Without a key the engine
# falls back to deterministic keyword scoring and template replies.
# ZAI_API_KEY=
# ZAI_API_BASE=https://api.z.ai/api/paas/v4
# ZAI_MODEL=glm-4-flash

# Ruleset file (JSON array of routing rules); omit to use the built-in set.
# ENGINE_RULES_FILE=./config/rules.json
